<article class="env-definition" id="063J">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/063J">Definition <span data-tag="063J">31.22.1</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be an immersion of schemes. Choose an open subscheme $U \subset X$ such that $i$ identifies $Z$ with a closed subscheme of $U$ and denote $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ U$ the corresponding quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>regular immersion</em> if $\mathcal{I}$ is regular. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>Koszul-regular immersion</em> if $\mathcal{I}$ is Koszul-regular. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>$H_1$-regular immersion</em> if $\mathcal{I}$ is $H_1$-regular. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $i$ is a <em>quasi-regular immersion</em> if $\mathcal{I}$ is quasi-regular. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>